type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* The expand/collapse buttons of the `toc` macros now carry `aria-label`s naming the entry, so screen readers announce them instead of an empty button (fixes [[Issue #9794|https://github.com/TiddlyWiki/TiddlyWiki5/issues/9794]])
* The label uses the `caption` field where there is one, falling back to the title. A caption written in wikitext is rendered first, so the label never contains raw markup
* TOC entries are wrapped in a `tc-toc-item-row` flex row; custom CSS that targets `.toc-item > a` for layout may need updating to the new class
* The `toc` macros use the `<%if%>` conditional instead of `$reveal` for expand/collapse state, so each entry renders fewer DOM elements
* TOC expand/collapse buttons carry `tc-toc-chevron`, their blank placeholders carry `tc-toc-chevron-blank`, and item links carry `tc-toc-link`, giving custom CSS stable hooks
